hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16034","Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said, Abd al-Malik ibn Jurayj informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, that Hisham ibn Yahya informed him that Ikrimah ibn Salamah ibn Rabiah informed him that two brothers of Banu al-Mughirah met Mujammi ibn Yazid al-Ansari and said, I bear witness that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that a neighbor not prevent his neighbor from fixing a timber in his wall. And the swearing one said, O my brother, I knew that judgment is for you, and I have sworn, so make a pillar short of my wall. So the other did, and fixed a timber in the pillar. Ibn Jurayj said, Amr said, and I looked at that."
"16035","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said, Ibn Jurayj, Amr ibn Dinar informed me, from Hisham ibn Yahya, he informed him that Ikrimah ibn Salamah ibn Rabiah informed him that two brothers of Banu al-Mughirah, one of them freed, that no timber be fixed in his wall, and they met Mujammi ibn Yazid al-Ansari and many men, and they said, we bear witness that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A neighbor shall not prevent his neighbor from fixing timber in his wall. And the swearing one said, O my brother, I knew that judgment is for you against me, and I have sworn, so make a pillar short of my wall. So the other did, and fixed a timber in the pillar. And Amr said to me, and I looked at that."
"16036","Harun narrated to us, he said, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said, Yazid ibn Iyad informed me, from Yazid ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ruqaysh, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jariyah, from Mujammi ibn Yazid ibn Jariyah, that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in sandals."
